# Line endings
#
# Every text file is stored in the repository with LF and checked out with LF,
# regardless of the platform the clone lives on. Before this was a catch-all,
# only the extensions listed under "build and script files" below were pinned,
# so a Windows clone left ~635 .ts/.tsx/.svg files permanently dirty with pure
# CRLF churn and `git status` became unreadable. `.gitattributes` beats
# core.autocrlf, so this holds no matter how a contributor's git is configured.
* text=auto eol=lf

# .bat is the one exception: cmd.exe wants CRLF, so it is stored LF and checked
# out CRLF. Declared explicitly, it does not show up as a modification.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Build and script files where LF is load-bearing, not just tidy: CRLF in a
# shebang or a Dockerfile becomes `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M` inside a Linux
# container. Redundant under the catch-all above, kept as documentation of why
# these in particular must never drift.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
docker-compose.*.yml text eol=lf
compose.yaml text eol=lf
compose.*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.env text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.cfg text eol=lf
*.ini text eol=lf

# Binary — never touched by line-ending conversion or diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.whl binary

*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
